      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-85897\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">4.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/2839#7503\">Computing the Probability of a Geometric Random Variable on an Unbounded Interval</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"85897\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>In a town, blood tests are being carried out on all inhabitants to determine whether they have caught a virus. On average, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"49\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c25\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> of the inhabitants test positive for the virus. What is the probability that the first positive test result will be made on the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"50\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>rd test or later? </p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Wed, Oct 14th @ 10:42 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:10</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></di